          ":question/math-academy-id": "q-20268",
          ":question/problem": "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+2y+z &=-4 \\\\ y+z &=-2 \\\\ z &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form.",
          ":question/worked-solution": "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNotice that the matrix $M$ is already in row echelon form.\n\nTransforming $M$ to reduced row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{3} \\\\  & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-1){R}_{3} \\\\  & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 0 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-2){R}_{2} \\\\  & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
