                ":question/problem": "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x-6y+2z &=8 \\\\ -6x+18y-6z &=-24 \\\\ 4x-12y+4z &=16\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form.",
                ":question/worked-solution": "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n\n$$\nM= \\left[ \\begin{array}{ccc|c}2 & -6 & 2 & 8 \\\\ -6 & 18 & -6 & -24 \\\\ 4 & -12 & 4 & 16\\end{array} \\right].\n$$\n\n\n\nTransforming $M$ to reduced row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -6 & 2 & 8 \\\\ -6 & 18 & -6 & -24 \\\\ 4 & -12 & 4 & 16\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & 1 & 4 \\\\ -6 & 18 & -6 & -24 \\\\ 4 & -12 & 4 & 16\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+6{R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 4 & -12 & 4 & 16\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-4){R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n\n$$\nM\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -3 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\n"
              },
